From a5a373859a2d46cf2cfbae969c88b113ae6aa676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:43:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xbmc: format the lines Hades added to Kodi's own files to the
 100 columns of .clang-format

git clang-format (clang-format 21.1.8 from Ubuntu's archive, Kodi's .clang-format) over the
lines added by the changes of this release that were not formatted yet, in 10 files of xbmc/, and the comment lines of the same added
lines that it leaves over 100 columns (ReflowComments is off) wrapped by hand, in 3 more.

Only layout changes: the tokens of every file are the same before and after (comments and
string literals compared without their line breaks) and so is the set of #include lines,
which clang-format puts in sorted order inside their blocks. The 213 compile commands of the
last Kodi build over the changed files and their dependents give the same result as before.
tools/dvbridge is not formatted: it is C in its own style, which .clang-format would
change to Kodi's C++ one.
